                   mhi_dev->mhi_cntrl->buffer_len, MHI_EOT);
if (rc)
    dev_err(&mhi_dev->dev, "Failed to recycle the buffer: %d\n", rc);
```
Reason:
Replacing `mhi_prepare_for_transfer_autoqueue()` with `mhi_prepare_for_transfer()` and manually queuing RX buffers via `qcom_mhi_qrtr_queue_dl_buffers()` gives the client driver full control over when buffers become active. This ensures that all driver structures are fully initialized before any `dl_callback` can occur. The `dl_callback` now also recycles each buffer after consumption, maintaining a continuous supply of RX buffers without relying on the MHI auto‑queue mechanism.

